      "problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=10\\ne 0.$",
